{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492906-if-galatea-happened-today","id":492906,"title":"If Galatea happened today.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-26T14:22:56-07:00","id":492906,"title":"If Galatea happened today.","content":"So I've been trying to put a story arc together to run some friends of mine though. I really want do a Day 0 sort of scenario, those initial groups of novas who erupted the day of or right after the Galatea explosion, but I really didn't want to deal with the keeping up with the old dates. I didn't initially really put much thought into what that meant, but now I'm sitting here thinking: We have a way different tech base that we did in 1998. Programs like 23andMe that groups like the Aeon society could mine for potential novas even before the Galatea happens. We live in a world were almost every one has a camera in there pocket. Nova eruptions will be posted on youtube and vines.<br /> <br /> Anyone else want to help me add to this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5371-sahugani","name":"Sahugani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5371_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T18:40:01-07:00","id":493107,"title":"","content":"data analysis. the use of big data and analytics would make it childs play to spot many newly erupted novas, even if they stayed hidden. because it would represent a change in patterns, and the various agencies would quickly build models to predict hidden novas with some percentage of accuracy and significance. if your cell phone moved too fast while on, thats a flag (but that could be other things). sudden changes in pattern right at the event may be other flags. add up enough flags and you know where to look. a sudden absence of data is also a flag, moreso if data was removed.<br /> <br /> at this point, op!net would be 'different' than the internet to avoid the current FCC regulation rather than any other reason. possibly engineered into a legal blind spot on purpose. eufiber would exist in about 3 years, so you have to wait for it a bit, but its probably a massive bandwidth increase.<br /> <br /> some nova would find all the backdoor hacks in our current OS that the required, and either abuse them or reveal them. or maybe both would happen. another nova would make a new secure OS and everyone would migrate to that platform. it would be a massive leaks situation for everyone.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4695-teulisch","name":"Teulisch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T20:46:53-07:00","id":493220,"title":"","content":"Assuming an organization like Aeon existed, they'd have to step way more lightly in today's world of paranoia. If they randomly picked out some nova to recruit, all it takes is a single tweet and the suspicion would start flying. In an era where people are just looking for some kind of civil rights violation to raise hell about, if they did anything other than send info for how to apply for a job, they would never crawl out from under the internet's scrutiny. Big media spectacles like they did in the previous timeline would be picked apart in comment forums, and internet news blogs. They'd take apart that news coverage of Randall Portman like a lego castle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T12:56:51-07:00","id":493877,"title":"","content":"Loads of UAV and microdrone spying on and monitoring of Novas, 25/8/366. You wouldn't dare let one of these walking potential nukes out of a government's sight for even a moment.<br /> <br /> On the flipside, given the advent of 9/11 and all the debacle since then, how many governments (especially the U.S.) would be jumping at the chance to contract with or recruit a Nova (or Novas) to fighting &quot;the war on terror&quot; for them, a la Doctor Manhattan single-handedly winning the Viet Nam war?<br /> <br /> Or better/worse yet, what about PMCs like Blackwater / Xe? (And consider the morality of those Novas who'd happily step into that kind of job.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 04-27-2015, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T13:24:24-07:00","id":493908,"title":"","content":"Elites, PMC novas fighting wars effectively by proxy, were always a thing, but I'd be surprised if they weren't more active. T2M would likely be more active in their peacekeeping roles too, perhaps run a bit ragged dealing with all of the various private and rogue elements.<br /> <br /> That said, I actually think that novas would stand the biggest chance of changing things for the better. If anything, the change between pre- and post-N Day could be even more jarring (and harder for humanity to want to part with, hence the Nippon issue in 2120) with all of the frankly awful things that have happened since Aberrant was first written. We could probably use a Superman (or Caestus Pax) more than before, and Utopia probably has even more room to make the world a better place since 1997.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4732-drazosh","name":"Drazosh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T14:20:32-07:00","id":493937,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the reminder on the Elites; I never got a chance to read through all the original storylines for Aberrant (I was more a Trinity person), so I missed some details. But I do seem to remember something about some Novas or their associates being killed in 'accidents' while working to improve the world around them. Also, some news about one Nova-monitoring agency deliberately sterilizing them (wasn't that part of what touched off the Aberrant War?). Considering the uproar people get into about reproductive rights (or the removal thereof) these days, major media sites and social networking would go ballistic with that sort of news.<br /> <br /> Also considering the more prevalent view of corporate oligarchy these days (see also Wall Street, Subprime mortgage crisis of 2008, etc; along with the fact that it's just not profitable to have a Utopia), I can imagine a lot of corporations either trying to leash Novas with lobbying to governments, legislation to keep them from getting in the way of corporate moneymaking, and so on.<br /> <br /> That, or hiring them on to put them to use for said corporation, or trying to pay them off so they DON'T create any sort of paradisical world for all the consumers. You can only sell people something if they're unhappy, after all . . .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 04-27-2015, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T17:40:24-07:00","id":494126,"title":"","content":"One of the perks of the Aeon Society and Project Utopia was to provide novas with an escape from that. The Project trained novas, helped them, and put them to work and, as a nonprofit with an admittedly staggering amount of resources and UN connections, they can do so relatively free of corporate interference. That said, since the new version is supposed to be based on the notion that Aeon is inherently good and all problems in the world can be solved, &quot;Aeon vs Corporate Greed&quot; will likely make an appearance as a source of conflict for the players. Aeon helps you, they cover your needs, and they ask you only to use your abilities to make the world a better place. Do you still have a price? How far will people go to find it? Can you maintain your humility and sanity with godlike power and the attempts to draw your favor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4732-drazosh","name":"Drazosh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T06:20:07-07:00","id":494683,"title":"","content":"&quot;On the flipside, given the advent of 9/11 and all the debacle since then, how many governments (especially the U.S.) would be jumping at the chance to contract with or recruit a Nova (or Novas) to fighting &quot;the war on terror&quot; for them, a la Doctor Manhattan single-handedly winning the Viet Nam war?&quot; -Zsander<br /> <br /> ^This right here, a LOT. There was a footnote in the Aberant core book about some military initiative started by the US that was essentially a nova strike force. With our ridiculously runaway military spending we'd be all over that in a heartbeat. It might start out like SHIELD, but it would quickly be just another glorified Gestapo.<br /> <br /> There's another thread talking about India Syndrome, which got me thinking about someone erupting in one of the various fundamentalist or extremist denominations here in the US. Imagine a westboro baptist nova, or one of those cults out in California.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:29:36-07:00","id":494856,"title":"","content":"Extrapolating from world populations...<br /> It make take up to three days for the first eruption to occur, when it does, the first eruption occurs in China and is female and is also somehow christian (statistics by themselves don't always make perfect sense), but the first nova caught on camera is in urban India, likely in a slum due to population density. By the time the US has its first Nova, India and China have four apiece, then Indonesia, etc... Novas begin leaving poorer countries for richer ones immediately. Within the first week, we not only have public novas but also novas who post videos of themselves defying physics.<br /> After the first month India and China, with ten native Novas each, are likely interacting with at least one of their Novas - whether this is peaceful or violent in each case will determine a lot. Given China's treatment of Novas in the material, it might be safe to assume their first contact doesn't go well - it would be concealed, uncovered, reported and then promptly forgotten by the next news cycle. The first videos of Nova eruptions are carefully edited phone recordings out of Chinese media - but soon after, India sees recorded eruptions going up onto the internet unedited. Given their advanced mental agility, some of these Novas are hitting the ground running with the ability to connect with each other over global distances - nascent Nova institutions begin to form before human governments can shift their bulk to adapt to the rapidly changing landscape.<br /> After ninety seven days, the world has one hundred novas. Both China and India have contributed thirty or more, the US has seen seven, many countries are seeing their own emerge. An arms race between India and China over who first wields the power of a nova on the battlefield begins. The first acts of Nova terror begin as oppressed minorities strike out against tyrants - likely bringing the world to the brink of revolution within the first four months as old defence structures are rendered mostly useless in the face of lone Nova terrorists/freedom fighters. Nova exclusive circles are found online, but go above the heads of most baselines.<br /> After the first year (if the war hasn't already started, likely in Kashmir or somewhere over the Himalayas if it has), India and China both boast generation of over a hundred native novas - the US has produced 28, but likely has a great number of Indian and Chinese Novas working either in the US or for an organization from the US. Companies like Devries and Kurotek are given incentive enough to get started as soon as the concept pops into their creators mind. Early nova dabbling in science, art and war are outperforming and re-imagining the human spirit in ways that leave the world almost completely in their thrall. Nobody watches baseline videos when Novas are free to create their own content online - youtube-like nova-made video is shown nearly 24/7 on many tv stations. Nova discussions of Opnet conversion are blown into a doomsday scenario by respected baselines unable to understand the technology.<br /> By the end of the first decade, consult the following list for roughly predicted minimum nova populations by country of origin:<br /> China 1221<br /> India 1160<br /> US 284<br /> Indonesia 224<br /> Brazil 181<br /> Pakistan 173<br /> Nigeria 158<br /> Bangladesh 141<br /> Russia 128<br /> Japan 113<br /> <br /> Basically it happens much like it does in the book still, but all apologies to the US, they don't get to go first this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  demographics... 04-28-2015, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:59:04-07:00","id":494879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492906-if-galatea-happened-today?p=494683#post494683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . . someone erupting in one of the various fundamentalist or extremist denominations here in the US. Imagine a westboro baptist nova, or one of those cults out in California.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't this where Wycoff and the Blight came from in Trinity too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T16:12:42-07:00","id":495353,"title":"","content":"The flip side of the post 9-11 world is that on actual N-Day the government is going to be shitting its pants assuming terrorist have suddenly struck everywhere at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T16:31:27-07:00","id":495372,"title":"","content":"@ Zsander; Wycoff was actually a part of the Teragen harvesters, he's even mentioned briefly in the Terat splatbook.<br /> <br /> @Nihilist; What's the chances China suffers massive setbacks at the onset with their first few novas rebelling against the conformist regime over there and then laying waste to whatever forces arrayed against them using over-the-top quantum powers?<br /> <br /> The nova-exclusive circles would easily become our modern day foundation for the Teragen; an online community composed fo disenfranchised or dissatisfied novas who question society as a whole. It might even become similar to a nova NAACP if a character like Mal never entered the picture.<br /> <br /> @Wolfgar; Oh yes, I can just envision the panic! A swarm of uncontrolled elements with powers exceeding a battalion? Yup that's cause for the panic button.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T17:48:10-07:00","id":495492,"title":"","content":"A few side-story ideas, though not necessarily based in technological developments, but more sociological:<br /> <br /> The <i>Galatea</i> incident (originally) happened in, what, 1997? The first component for the I.S.S., meanwhile, was launched in 1998. If <i>Galatea </i>happened at this point, that makes me wonder how matters would resolve in the I.S.S.\u2014especially if someone aboard went Nova. (Or was that something that was described to have happened to MIR station in the original Aberrant timeline?)<br /> <br /> The W.B.C. mention earlier made me wonder about how they'd see Novas. Probably as yet something else to protest about and try to raise ire etc. Although <i>one</i> pissed off super going ballistic over a &quot;God Hates Novas&quot; sign would probably settle the whole mess right quick. Then again, what if one of the WBC <i>was</i> a Nova?<br /> <br /> Also, groups like Anonymous (or others) and their behaviors would be an interesting thing to bounce off Novas, especially those who strive to keep their identities (and families and such) secret. Considering how quick Anons or 4Channers or other hacktivists can work en masse to dox and harass regular people, one wonders how it would work out once they turned their collective attention to one of the Novas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T19:16:59-07:00","id":495628,"title":"","content":"There would also be Anonymous Novas as well. Almost anyone can be Anonymous. Also Pro-and Anti Nova subreddits, nova twitters, nova handler twitters, fake nova twitters, nova stalking on Pintrest, and tumblrs dedicated to being Novakin and having Nova headmates.<br /> <br /> North Korea is going to be a really different place if part of the ruling regime doesn't erupt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T20:07:07-07:00","id":495666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492906-if-galatea-happened-today?p=495628#post495628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There would also be Anonymous Novas as well. Almost anyone can be Anonymous.</div> </div> </div> </div>But as soon as you claim to be part of Anonymous, you're no longer Anonymous, per se . . . and being a Nova isn't exactly an anonymous thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> . . . Unless, perhaps, they somehow chose to act completely as an avatar of said organization, acting in its majority (?) interests, maintaining an appearance to match the suited, masked iconic Anon, and divesting themselves entirely of any other personal identity. Hm. Interesting idea, that . . .<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T08:31:11-07:00","id":497464,"title":"","content":"Anonymous Novas sounds like the beginning of Elite Mask-culture to me... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It came up as a question in one of my home games, but what would the most common power set be in our world today? If we assume the same principle for determining abilities (i.e. wish fulfillment during reactive planck-moment) how many more would be outrage or violence based in modern times?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T08:51:08-07:00","id":497506,"title":"","content":"Probably techno/cyberkinesis, or whatever it's called. At least amongst the younger generation - who might also gravitate toward untested Nova-centric philosophies (like the Teragen) as an alternative to any imperfections perceived in society - even when the Novas aren't actually concerned for the human part of the puzzle. A number of countries might see early domestic nova terrorism due to increased concentration of wealth/power and greater number of disenfranchised - but not likely enough to get the aberrant war started early, unless it concentrates in Kashmir/Jerusalem or some other sensitive flashpoint.<br /> That first month or so before the Zurich Accord comes into place would be pretty hairy business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T11:04:35-07:00","id":497639,"title":"","content":"Would our world today even bother with the Zurich Accord? It seems more likely that they'd find a way to classify such abilities as some kind of inherent weapon and try to limit them accordingly rather than quibble over the vague definition of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T11:49:27-07:00","id":497672,"title":"","content":"Novas can be very persuasive...<br /> It serves both species to have a kind of contract between them, i think one mega-social, mega-mental with a you-tube account could very easily sway human opinion to levels that would be politically unteneble to resist. Particularly in those early days, when Nova voices are so few.<br /> The attempt to control or restrict erupted citizens will just leave a bad taste in their mouth and see them fly away to greener pastures or become antagonistic, so most governments will try the carrot before they try the stick. In the early days at least, any country that isn't China or India will have a limited number of Novas and they will be as rare treasures to lower density countries. No need to disenfranchise them when they can serve as national assets and icons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T17:37:47-07:00","id":498032,"title":"","content":"I also see that, especially in today's environment, that the world would want to embrace novas. They would not see them as hideous monsters to be frightened of but yet another marginalized race that needs to be protected and nurtured. The world no longer is an X-Men world where the world would hate and fear them. No. I think that with the social upheavals that have occurred in recent times, the world would be a much better place for novas to &quot;erupt out of the closet&quot; so to speak. <br /> I think that any country that denies human rights would quickly see their most physically powerful citizens up and taking off. Or else it would spark some really ugly confrontations, which then would get plastered over Twitter and Youtube. From there, the countries would face the same problems they have in the past. Except now, they would have to deal with some of those protestors able to juggle the tanks the government would send.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T18:43:20-07:00","id":498084,"title":"","content":"We mustn't forget that novas have value as well. Not every nova shoots lasers and punches tractor trailers into pancakes. They can be the greatest athletes, artists, and scientists the world has ever known. They can easily perform the jobs of dozens, if not hundreds, of baselines single-handedly. Every corporation would love to have a nova or twelve on their rosters. They are a resource, and one that even countries with a history of human rights violations would not want to lose. Perhaps the best way to get novas to stay and help their motherland? Treat them like gold. Giving Superman basic human rights, then, is a small price to pay to have Superman as a productive and tax-paying citizen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4732-drazosh","name":"Drazosh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T19:17:46-07:00","id":498115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492906-if-galatea-happened-today?p=498032#post498032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also see that, especially in today's environment, that the world would want to embrace novas. They would not see them as hideous monsters to be frightened of but yet another marginalized race that needs to be protected and nurtured. The world no longer is an X-Men world where the world would hate and fear them. No. I think that with the social upheavals that have occurred in recent times, the world would be a much better place for novas to &quot;erupt out of the closet&quot; so to speak.<br /> I think that any country that denies human rights would quickly see their most physically powerful citizens up and taking off. Or else it would spark some really ugly confrontations, which then would get plastered over Twitter and Youtube. From there, the countries would face the same problems they have in the past. Except now, they would have to deal with some of those protestors able to juggle the tanks the government would send.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drazosh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492906-if-galatea-happened-today?p=498084#post498084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We mustn't forget that novas have value as well. Not every nova shoots lasers and punches tractor trailers into pancakes. They can be the greatest athletes, artists, and scientists the world has ever known. They can easily perform the jobs of dozens, if not hundreds, of baselines single-handedly. Every corporation would love to have a nova or twelve on their rosters. They are a resource, and one that even countries with a history of human rights violations would not want to lose. Perhaps the best way to get novas to stay and help their motherland? Treat them like gold. Giving Superman basic human rights, then, is a small price to pay to have Superman as a productive and tax-paying citizen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not nearly so certain that the real world of 2015 would so readily embrace novas. Yes, a great many nations around the world, whether democratic or totalitarian, would see the values of novas and make a rational decision to try to stay on their good side. But there are more than a few nations whose leaders are less than rational. I could definitely see places like Pakistan, Iran and Saudi Arabia (countries not known for respecting minority or equal rights) or transnational religio-political movements like ISIS turning against novas <i>en masse</i> if the religious leaders of those countries or organizations decided that novas were &quot;servants of the Devil.&quot; Religiously-inspired persecution has never been rational and can even play against the persecutors' best interests. Yes, novas could be of immense value to any country, but if the country in question's population becomes convinced that novas are inherently evil, then those novas will either have to fight against their native countrymen trying to persecute them or leave for greener pastures. The practical value of the novas wouldn't be able to outweigh the religious fanatical desire of &quot;purging the Devil's minions&quot; in these places. Drazosh is quite right that countries with rational leaders would bend over backwards to accommodate their novas. My point is that there are more than a few countries whose religious fanatics would demand that the novas should at the least be kicked out or at worst captured and executed &quot;to fulfill God's will&quot; and never mind the immense benefits they could bring to their nations. Even if the leaders of such countries saw the benefits of having novas under their sway, if the majority of the population was fanatically opposed to novas, that opposition would make accommodating novas politically untenable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 04-30-2015, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T20:13:21-07:00","id":498147,"title":"","content":"I agree with Su-Tehp. ISIS, and others mentioned along with any number of at least in America Evangelical Churches would instantly condem Novas. The Church of St. Michael in the setting is a good depiction of one such group. Another issue that should probably be looked at is income inequality and the effect it would have on Novas. It is a major issue for people who for instance win the lottery or become major sport stars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T04:49:18-07:00","id":498637,"title":"","content":"I was kind of surprised to see the numbers for religious populations in 2015 - i thought there was more secularism out there honestly. So there will definitely be faithful religious Novas, perhaps even more reliably than patriotic nationalist Novas. But one would hope that both faiths make enough noise about peace for Nova adherrants to not go medieval on us. I think any faith claiming the Nova standing in the aisle is a false idol, while holding up their own ancient human traditions may find themselves in a race they can't win - i see new dogma and tenets being a fascinating avenue of debate amongst theologists post n-day, perhaps even hearing a bit from newly erupted in the exploration.<br /> -shrug-<br /> <br /> While certain outliers will exist, nearly all modern nations will try to woo their Novas to stay rather than provoke them. At least one serious revolution behind a Nova figurehead would be happening in many of the nastiest tyrannies about the world. Some tension may even be created solely by Novas out for the 'lolz' - humiliating whole baseline authorities with seemingly little effort. But after a single month, Aeon steps in to negotiate for the UN - probably quicker in the modern speed of news cycles - after a month no more than 80 or so eruptions have occured across the world - less if Aeon acts quicker. I could see a few countries executing a number of Nova citizens in military actions against them - but this won't hold back the tide for long, driving new eruptees underground and out of sight if they decide to stay at all.<br /> If anywhere gets badly hit by N-Day, it might very well be the US - the country has really made a mess of its international standing over the past decade or so. An international consortium of Novas might take action against their perceived oppressors - while some of these conglomerates might sanction violence, i feel a large enough group would tend toward peaceful restructuring of global US hegemony, at least at first. Eventually there will almost certainly be a post N-Day attack on the US - but for all their power and money, they simply can't risk the global community of Novas getting any more fed up with them and will be hesitant to engage their (still) fearsome hard power.<br /> The US isn't entirely alone here, but the disapproval ratings they face in these last few years is kind of unprecedented - France, Russia and Britain may also see blow-back parrallel to the US - due to their colonial ways. The trend of international recruits making their way into ISIS/ISIL could easily parrallel a rise in violent nova activism against US interests from across the world. Unlike ISIS/ISIL, the beneficiary nation(s) to all these Novas would probably prosper - it could be a stronger clarion call than that of the Zurich Accord if left long enough.<br /> Frighteningly, this kind of accumulation of disenfranchised Novas into the middle east seems to me to have been one of the ultimate causes of the aberrant war in 2049, but for it to already begin in 2015 without the early optimistic years of 1998-2008 to set a solid foundation from. The risk of escalation is much more immediate and dire if this occurs.<br /> -shiver-<br /> Elsewhere, China will almost certainly see the first Nova joining the Peoples Army, simply based on the numbers involved. I can't recall what happens to it in the canon setting, but Taiwan will probably see the first national nova military (soft power) action within the first few years - leaving China one-up against the US in the post N-Day pacific theatre. Soon afterwards, the Himalayas will see tensions between China and India as India starts operations in Kashmir - all soft power endeavours in the early days - made very effective by Nova contributions. The entire power structure of the world is going to shift to China and India quickly - because there is no chance of any other country matching their rates of new Novas and the global nova sentiment against US hard power preventing the US from effectively containing the eastern powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  hard and soft power 05-01-2015, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T11:13:21-07:00","id":499134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492906-if-galatea-happened-today?p=498115#post498115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not nearly so certain that the real world of 2015 would so readily embrace novas. Yes, a great many nations around the world, whether democratic or totalitarian, would see the values of novas and make a rational decision to try to stay on their good side. But there are more than a few nations whose leaders are less than rational. I could definitely see places like Pakistan, Iran and Saudi Arabia (countries not known for respecting minority or equal rights) or transnational religio-political movements like ISIS turning against novas <i>en masse</i> if the religious leaders of those countries or organizations decided that novas were &quot;servants of the Devil.&quot; Religiously-inspired persecution has never been rational and can even play against the persecutors' best interests. Yes, novas could be of immense value to any country, but if the country in question's population becomes convinced that novas are inherently evil, then those novas will either have to fight against their native countrymen trying to persecute them or leave for greener pastures. The practical value of the novas wouldn't be able to outweigh the religious fanatical desire of &quot;purging the Devil's minions&quot; in these places. Drazosh is quite right that countries with rational leaders would bend over backwards to accommodate their novas. My point is that there are more than a few countries whose religious fanatics would demand that the novas should at the least be kicked out or at worst captured and executed &quot;to fulfill God's will&quot; and never mind the immense benefits they could bring to their nations. Even if the leaders of such countries saw the benefits of having novas under their sway, if the majority of the population was fanatically opposed to novas, that opposition would make accommodating novas politically untenable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, don't get me wrong, there would be some fanatics who would make life difficult, particularly in the countries you mentioned. Novas would likely leave these countries in droves (insofar as there could possibly be &quot;droves&quot; of a limited population), and those governments would suffer for their lack. That said, those nations also have a bit of a reputation for lying to their people, and it would not shock me if each had a &quot;secret asset&quot; or two on the payroll.<br /> <br /> The world at large, though, would view it as just another arms' race. Internally, privately, they may hate novas and do everything possible to keep them under foot and manageable, but the corporations and governments who see their value will try pretty hard to keep their opinions to themselves. The Directive would almost certainly be a thing, maybe even faster and with more support than the original timeline, but they'd likely stick more to the shadows to make sure public opinion didn't swing the other way. One news story of a nova getting shot in official custody, as we have unfortunately seen of late, would make their work very difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4732,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4732-drazosh","user":"Drazosh","date":". 05-01-2015, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4732-drazosh","name":"Drazosh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:22:54-07:00","id":499249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492906-if-galatea-happened-today?p=498637#post498637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anywhere gets badly hit by N-Day, it might very well be the US - the country has really made a mess of its international standing over the past decade or so. An international consortium of Novas might take action against their perceived oppressors - while some of these conglomerates might sanction violence, i feel a large enough group would tend toward peaceful restructuring of global US hegemony, at least at first. Eventually there will almost certainly be a post N-Day attack on the US - but for all their power and money, they simply can't risk the global community of Novas getting any more fed up with them and will be hesitant to engage their (still) fearsome hard power..</div> </div> </div> </div>^^This right here is the seed for both the Directive and an all-American nova-military initiative in our time. If there is anything that is certain about our government it's that it can;t abide the thought of not being on top of the hill as far as international military force. And they'll devote our bloated, runaway military budget (80% of our GNP) towards training the most lethal force of novas in the world. Especially if ANY sort of reprisal comes from overseas in the form of nova-violence. It would effectively trigger another 9/11 scenario that would make us even more paranoid and distrustful of other nations, particularly if those other nations can send humanoid armies at us at any time. The US would become an Orwellian nightmare overnight after the first reprisal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T14:15:52-07:00","id":499380,"title":"","content":"Not to put too fine a point on it, but... That sounds an awful lot like the foundations for Trinity/Aeon's FSA to me. That, I'd say, is perhaps the most telling thing of all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4732,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4732-drazosh","user":"Drazosh","date":". 05-01-2015, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4732-drazosh","name":"Drazosh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T21:01:56-07:00","id":499731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drazosh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492906-if-galatea-happened-today?p=499380#post499380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to put too fine a point on it, but... That sounds an awful lot like the foundations for Trinity/Aeon's FSA to me. That, I'd say, is perhaps the most telling thing of all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was gonna post something to this effect as well, but Drazosh beat me to it because I was busy posting on the Werewolf: the Apocalypse forum about having just read the FATAL and Friends review of the Children of Gaia Revised tribebook. I knew people have been hating on TB: CoG ever since it was published and, having never read the book, I didn't know what all the fuss was about.<br /> <br /> Now I know.<br /> <br /> But I wish I didn't. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">(SWEET MERCIFUL GAWDS, MY EYES!) </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Let me put it this way: I'm very tempted to change my signature to state how the first tenet of the Litany <i>clearly does not have a buttsecks exception</i> but for the notion that to quote myself in my own signature seems to me to be in very poor taste.<br /> <br /> We apologize for any inconvenience and now return you to your regularly scheduled Trinity forum programming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 05-02-2015, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T02:51:56-07:00","id":500068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492906-if-galatea-happened-today?p=499249#post499249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ^^This right here is the seed for both the Directive and an all-American nova-military initiative in our time. If there is anything that is certain about our government it's that it can;t abide the thought of not being on top of the hill as far as international military force. And they'll devote our bloated, runaway military budget (80% of our GNP) towards training the most lethal force of novas in the world. Especially if ANY sort of reprisal comes from overseas in the form of nova-violence. It would effectively trigger another 9/11 scenario that would make us even more paranoid and distrustful of other nations, particularly if those other nations can send humanoid armies at us at any time. The US would become an Orwellian nightmare overnight after the first reprisal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't ever read the Directive sourcebook as closely as i should have because it was my brother's setting to play with in our arrangements - if fact i probably shouldn't be saying much in here because i don't know Aberrant's setting as well as its rules. But i do keep an eye on global affairs, so this thread is like an open flame to a moth for me - appealing but dangerous grounds...<br /> <br /> Behind the scenes, the nations of the world could be drawing up frantic military actions and vowing to yoke or kill every last one of them, but the US has a hell of a lot of people 'behind the scenes' like Snowden and might be vulnerable to global disapproval spreading to global nova populations. Continuing to listen to money over populations will become increading indefensible and risky, history is pretty clear in this regard. Novas will immediately redefine 'the priviledged few', they can get money, those with money can't as easily obtain M-R nodes.<br /> I would posit that the US might actually be forced to re-evaluate some of their positions immediately or be held accountable by a nascent, global Nova alliance - their soft-power economic and cultural capacity will serve them much better than anything so easily despicted as super-villainy in a time of super-heroes. The tropes involved were almost all created in their own country after-all - it's hard to imagine any but the first generation of belligerent post N-Day senators, congressmen and other leaders misunderstanding the monumental changes to the planet so badly. All of those voices will be removed from power by a populace curled around social media Nova fingers at the earliest convenience, democracies will be the playthings of amateur nova social engineers unless something is done about the internet.<br /> But the Opnet is a Nova invention from the canon, so despite some surface layer tools designed to keep human law-makers and censors happy, the new system is designed for quantum interactions ultimately and free of deeper human accessibility. Still, that's years away from N-Day - but the ability for Mega-Social and Mental to spread memetically across the internet is a powerful motivator for such a public democracy as the US to pull its head back in fast. There just isn't anything to really compare it to, off the top of my head - a handful of Nova voices joined in encouragement could start a civil rights movement and it could be done in seconds over Twitter or a similar platform.<br /> This may need to be demonstrated a few times before the really entrenched finally give in, but that many motivated people can be very difficult to ignore in a true democracy. A nova with the right anima could get very hot and be more universally admired than any baseline, presenting an unassailable political opponent with a message that comes right to your handheld-device. Even under the deluge of corporate money now involved, outspeaking that nova with the additional power of a social media could be impossible without a nova spokesperson of your own, prior to the Zurich Accord even that isn't an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T08:05:48-07:00","id":500354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492906-if-galatea-happened-today?p=498115#post498115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could definitely see places like Pakistan, Iran and Saudi Arabia (countries not known for respecting minority or equal rights) or transnational religio-political movements like ISIS turning against novas <i>en masse</i> if the religious leaders of those countries or organizations decided that novas were &quot;servants of the Devil.&quot; Religiously-inspired persecution has never been rational and can even play against the persecutors' best interests. Yes, novas could be of immense value to any country, but if the country in question's population becomes convinced that novas are inherently evil, then those novas will either have to fight against their native countrymen trying to persecute them or leave for greener pastures. The practical value of the novas wouldn't be able to outweigh the religious fanatical desire of &quot;purging the Devil's minions&quot; in these places. Drazosh is quite right that countries with rational leaders would bend over backwards to accommodate their novas. My point is that there are more than a few countries whose religious fanatics would demand that the novas should at the least be kicked out or at worst captured and executed &quot;to fulfill God's will&quot; and never mind the immense benefits they could bring to their nations. Even if the leaders of such countries saw the benefits of having novas under their sway, if the majority of the population was fanatically opposed to novas, that opposition would make accommodating novas politically untenable.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a lot harder to oppress people with actual power. It's also a lot different to throw out &quot;devils&quot; when they can level a city block.<br /> <br /> I believe the expression of the nova in these cases is really going to determine how these groups react, more so than the fact of being a nova. Novas who have largely beneficial powers, or who are largely human+, will be accepted over novas who are largely destructive or seem particularly inhuman. Novas who stay humble and show strong faith will likely be accepted. I see more prohibitions against individual novas (Divis Mal definitely), than restrictions on novas as a whole.<br /> <br /> Also, I hesitate to think religious leaders are completely irrational. More than one decision seems to be based purely on cementing political power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T09:58:14-07:00","id":500520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492906-if-galatea-happened-today?p=500354#post500354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a lot harder to oppress people with actual power. It's also a lot different to throw out &quot;devils&quot; when they can level a city block.</div> </div> </div> </div>Harder, yes, but not impossible. Even a nova who can level a city block is still vulnerable to a <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ZergRush\" target=\"_blank\">Zerg Rush</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492906-if-galatea-happened-today?p=500354#post500354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the expression of the nova in these cases is really going to determine how these groups react, more so than the fact of being a nova. Novas who have largely beneficial powers, or who are largely human+, will be accepted over novas who are largely destructive or seem particularly inhuman. Novas who stay humble and show strong faith will likely be accepted. I see more prohibitions against individual novas (Divis Mal definitely), than restrictions on novas as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>All other things being equal, this is entirely correct. But history is replete with examples of political leaders whipping up the masses to persecute harmless people just for being different. It even happens today, even (especially?) in the US. (Just take a look at conservative preachers bitching and moaning about the inevitability of gay marriage. Some of them have said some really hateful things in the past few days since the Obergafel case was argued at the Supreme Court on Tuesday.) And you can't get much more different from the rest of the human race than having superpowers. And it <i>really doesn't</i> take a lot of effort to turn a bunch of weak-minded believers into a mob. Don't forget what the legends say happened to that dude with the initials &quot;J.C.&quot;. (or &quot;I.C.&quot; or &quot;INRI&quot; <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AltumVidetur?from=Main.GratuitousLatin\" target=\"_blank\">in the Latin</a>.) According to legend, he was a really nice guy and he had superpowers and he didn't hesitate to use them for the good of the people and he <i>still </i>got killed by a mob (or rather a mob turned him in to a sham court and he got a railroaded verdict and <i>then </i>he was executed) because they were somehow convinced he was a threat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492906-if-galatea-happened-today?p=500354#post500354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I hesitate to think religious leaders are completely irrational. More than one decision seems to be based purely on cementing political power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, true as you tell it. There are a number of religious leaders who <i>are </i>rational and <i>do </i>make decisions on the basis of cementing political power. But I expect you'll find a not-insignificant number of true believers among their number who would gladly destroy themselves if they could take their (perceived) enemies down with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 05-02-2015, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T10:20:16-07:00","id":500529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492906-if-galatea-happened-today?p=500520#post500520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All other things being equal, this is entirely correct. But history is replete with examples of political leaders whipping up the masses to persecute harmless people just for being different.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't really call novas &quot;harmless&quot; though. Again, novas have power, and not just combat power. It's very easy to leverage quantum abilities into financial advantage and social advantage. You can decree all you want but no one is going to want to believe a Mega-Charismatic nova is anything but devout.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It even happens today, even (especially?) in the US. (Just take a look at conservative preachers bitching and moaning about the inevitability of gay marriage. Some of them have said some really hateful things in the past few days since the Obergafel case was argued at the Supreme Court on Tuesday.) </div> </div> </div>Not especially in the US, no. In the US, definitely, but not especially. A vocal subgroup wanting to ban a certain form of legal construct and failing pretty compares poorly to a majority demanding a death penalty and succeeding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you can't get much more different from the rest of the human race than having superpowers. And it <i>really doesn't</i> take a lot of effort to turn a bunch of weak-minded believers into a mob. </div> </div> </div>It also doesn't take much turn a mob around, or scare the shit out of them. Collective action is really, really quite hard to achieve.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't forget what the legends say happened to that dude with the initials &quot;J.C.&quot;. (or &quot;I.C.&quot; or &quot;INRI&quot; <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AltumVidetur?from=Main.GratuitousLatin\" target=\"_blank\">in the Latin</a>.) According to legend, he was a really nice guy and he had superpowers and he didn't hesitate to use them for the good of the people and he <i>still </i>got killed by a mob (or rather a mob turned him in to a sham court and he got a railroaded verdict and <i>then </i>he was executed) because they were somehow convinced he was a threat. </div> </div> </div>I have two narratives on that:<br /> <br /> 1) He didn't have divine powers, so they weren't really relevant to saving him or<br /> <br /> 2) He had superpowers, but getting killed was the whole point of the exercise<br /> <br /> The upshot being, you cannot make a divinely powered being doing something they don't want to do unless you yourself are also a divinely powered being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T11:43:58-07:00","id":500566,"title":"","content":"The US will have it kind of easy compared to hardline nations (China comes to mind), because in the US the illusion (at least) of public discourse is maintained giving the impression that change can be achieved peacefully from the inside. Sure, you'll have your margin of extremists - we always do, but their voices will ring hollow next to a mega-social, their words will fall flat when directed against a mega-mental and they'll be ridiculed by serious society at large. When voices of authority raise against a popular godling in a democratic setting, the godling will be presented with the opportunity to redress the concerns. If not on the same stage, then by means of internet or word of mouth - both options are enhanced by the nova's state, and maybe their anima/powerset also.<br /> I can see military footage of a nova being killed being 'accidentally' leaked to news agencies at least (if not made public), not for broadcast, but just as a reality check. The first footage would almost certainly come from China, but if it happened in India - the world could be hearing about it in the same day. Fear will be as equal a motivator as wonder in the early going - so i can understand Su-tehp's insistence on the threat of government - but before the US has even a single Nova, China will have four. The US will already have some idea of what to expect from diplomatic and intelligence information - plus, the US soft power is so strong that even young Novas can be taken in by it's lure - as long as the ones in charge aren't assholes they may avoid domestic Novas troubles for a year or more if it's done well. If, and it's a big if, the US behaves itself and acts according to its founding principles - it can still be the best country in the world, it's all up to the personalities you want in charge.<br /> I can tell you that our Prime Minister in Australia (where i am) would do everything in his power to attach N-Day to his failing polls to gain some approval back, but would almost inevitably look the buffoon again when the first Australian Nova is of immigrant descent or something. Maybe if someone else came to power they might be able to repair the shattered trust from the shameful past few decade of politics here - but i have a hard time imagining my government being more persuasive than the contries first nova. But we wouldn't have a nova of our own for months, so a level of anticipation and expectations on whoever we got first would be sufficient to make them an overnight celebrity here.<br /> I could see Indian and Chinese efforts to police their eruptees leading to undergrounds, if the US played its cards right, those undergrounds would funnel to them - meaning the incentive is too great to be squandered. Britain, France and other european nations would be right behind the US picking up any disenfrachised novas they miss. If you want the story of fear, look to China and India - their nova populations are going to be obscene and many developments are going to be happening there first by pure numeric volume. Imagine the poor Taiwanese waiting for the first Chinese supermen to start touching down, or Kashmiris waiting for the Indian counterparts. Imagine the Tibetans or any other flashpoint between the two, knowing that the nations could very well go to nuclear, super-powered war over them given sufficient provocation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T11:46:17-07:00","id":500576,"title":"","content":"In the original cannon they had an example of some nova erupting and obliterating an entire mob of fanatics with silver fires, I'd wonder how many times that might happen before people realize that zerg-rush while clustered is not a great idea, but...fanaticism is already an expression of one's lack of higher rational skills.<br /> <br /> So given mega-charismatic novas and sufficiently political-minded novas with combat/utility powers, in our world how long until a scenario like &quot;Dominion&quot; from World Wide Phase 2 comes about? The novas there wanted to take over the Ukraine but i can see that kind of thing springing up in other 3rd world areas, particularly in parts of the African continent that are ravaged by warlords, or burnt out South-american countries where the government is really just an organized drug cartel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":765,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","user":"Darksol-aeternium","date":". 05-02-2015, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T22:33:04-07:00","id":501381,"title":"","content":"I suspect that's exactly the kind of thing that Utopia/T2M and similar groups will have to face. The world is big, novas are powerful, and it's impossible to apply a universal prediction to anyone's reactions. Some will undoubtedly try the kind of coup that took place in World Wide Phase 2, Elites will be called in, Team Tomorrow and various municipal defenders will work to establish some order, and another catastrophe will take its place. One could argue that this is a typical conceit of the superhero genre, the treadmill of heroics and the tragedies that make them necessary, but this is equally a fact of the world. Problems happen, people fix them (or don't), but the world as a whole - and humanity's capacity to rain bile on itself - stubbornly resists improvement as much as it can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4732-drazosh","name":"Drazosh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T14:13:06-07:00","id":502160,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you mentioned those (the Municipal Defenders). On one hand they will become absolutely necessary if a city wants to survive the predations of a criminal nova population, but on the other hand wouldn't the baseline police become resentful of having to play second fiddle to a &quot;super-cop&quot;? It doesn't help that the police reputation here in the US is less than sterling, people here might react to a super powered cop with suspicion as they're even less controllable. The option does exist for a whole community to gang up on and eliminate a corrupt cop (assuming the people are properly motivated), but that's not a guarantee with a suitably powered nova.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T19:30:35-07:00","id":502389,"title":"","content":"Honestly I don't think nova-criminals are going to be a big thing. Like, if you have to resort to drug-dealing or robbing banks to make money as a nova, you are seriously wasting your potential. Now, nova terrorists are likely going to be a problem, but that's a different ball of wax. A rebellious nova isn't a police matter; they're a cross between an act of war and a natural disaster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T19:30:46-07:00","id":503733,"title":"","content":"While I could see Organized Crime having Novas depending on the country I would think most Nova law enforcement would end up in a national police force the FBI or Scotland Yard for examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T21:46:20-07:00","id":503810,"title":"","content":"Purely by the numbers, at least two of the United States potential novas will be in prison when they erupt (about the same as in North Korea), roughly four more will be illegal immigrants (if that counts for anything). Otherwise, criminal populations are too low and too political to draw up an early nova underworld - but i already mentioned that an underground would be forming in the most populated areas and that will fit the future nova underworld like a glove when their time comes.<br /> Municipal defenders would probably be an entirely American concept, so if the inhabitants of that great land don't see it being viable anymore then i would have to digress - certainly the local police novas of the 2008 setting were a major force in the formation of nova criminal syndicates from the Underworld supplement. So Nova crime-fighting is (maybe camply) written into the canon and may require a substitute for the defenders role in that drama. That book gives some fair reasoning for Novas to visit the other side of the tracks - but even it admits it takes some time to build up a head of steam.<br /> In a way, it seems to me that municipal defenders might still make the cut prior to the slow pace that an FBI or Scotland yard might make toward a nova-inclusive approach - just for the sake of expediency. Quicker to invite a local nova in and get them on the payroll if you are a local leader, federal actions are generally much more belaboured and beaureacratic, states will be able to move quicker and cities quickest - as long as individual corruption didn't slow them down. Inevitably their baseline police counterparts will feel sidelined and useless, but there just isn't the Nova population for every 'city' to have a nova on staff, so they'll mostly be novelties and PR stunts. But there could be a market there for a DeVries (or similar) to privately contract to cities, for special occasions or needs. Maybe cities will own the 'mask' and identity, but the novas playing the role are interchangable, sometimes even substituted with baseline actors for mundane appearances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T16:01:18-07:00","id":504701,"title":"","content":"<br /> <i>\u201cPurely by the numbers, at least two of the United States potential novas will be in prison when they erupt (about the same as in North Korea), roughly four more will be illegal immigrants (if that counts for anything). Otherwise, criminal populations are too low and too political to draw up an early nova underworld - but i already mentioned that an underground would be forming in the most populated areas and that will fit the future nova underworld like a glove when their time comes.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Given the existence of the American prison-industrial complex (i.e. the NEW slavery\u2026) I would have put the minimum higher. A significant amount of our eruptees may even have family shoved away in prison on some trumped-up charge.<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cMaybe cities will own the 'mask' and identity, but the novas playing the role are interchangable, sometimes even substituted with baseline actors for mundane appearances.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> The first time some big-name baseline actor gets pasted by a nova rival on live national television that idea will be completely scrapped. Can\u2019t you just see the media frenzy when Tom Cruise gets obliterated by some ignorant nova unaware that his \u201crival\u201d is simply being impersonated?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T03:47:34-07:00","id":505203,"title":"","content":"You are welcome to check my numbers, the fact that the US can reliably count on Novas erupting in prison is only paralleled by North Korea and that seemed poignant to the shift into nova criminality. But the actual numbers i figured were low based off the loose information i found on the first page of a google search. If i could get a 'total global prisoner' number and it gave me a similar result - i would stand by my assumptions - but my math is by no means definitive. 707 out of every 100,000 just isn't that much (if those numbers are right), although as a convict population it's an alarming number.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492906-if-galatea-happened-today?p=504701#post504701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first time some big-name baseline actor gets pasted by a nova rival on live national television that idea will be completely scrapped. Can\u2019t you just see the media frenzy when Tom Cruise gets obliterated by some ignorant nova unaware that his \u201crival\u201d is simply being impersonated?</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that there might be an actor that plays Kikjak on local childrens programming, or a look-alike that attends public events that the Nova in question might prefer to avoid. Anyone who dresses a baseline as a nova and expects them to fill the shoes is lacking in foresight to put it mildly. But, in a few cases, the identity is more valuable than the nova under it for certain purposes.The public defender as mascot, paid for with public perception in mind, not crimefighting.<br /> -shrug-<br /> Places and organizations may even hoax eruptions in the early years for reasons of defense and prestige (wouldn't put it past ISIS, Israel and Russia) - using elaborate CGI visual effects that would attract conspiracy theorists to analyze every occurance and even deny all eruptions uniformly. It may take a bit of time (weeks) for the first overseas studies of Chinese and Indian novas to be validated by the more celebrated universities in the western world - leading to more skepticism for the earliest reports. The hoax numbers could be skewed to present a world with far less novas, or alternately a world when one nation has more than it actually does in comparison to others (might be up North Korea's alley if their Nova expats haven't returned to liberate their people yet).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Hoax eruptions 05-06-2015, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T07:12:43-07:00","id":509838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492906-if-galatea-happened-today?p=504701#post504701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the existence of the American prison-industrial complex (i.e. the NEW slavery\u2026) I would have put the minimum higher. A significant amount of our eruptees may even have family shoved away in prison on some trumped-up charge.</div> </div> </div> </div>That will likely mean one or two nova escapees from prison, although I imagine they would likely go on towards prison reform than major crime sprees, as the bulk would be low level drug offenders. Some might be quite angry though. I can also see a potential Dirty Dozen/Suicide Squad style of deal with the government as well; novas are too valuable a resource to just let rot in a prison cell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Municipal defenders would probably be an entirely American concept, so if the inhabitants of that great land don't see it being viable anymore then I would have to digress - certainly the local police novas of the 2008 setting were a major force in the formation of nova criminal syndicates from the Underworld supplement. </div> </div> </div>America would do it, but I can see the Japanese getting on board too, although likely in a radically different style.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T08:44:07-07:00","id":509869,"title":"","content":"I can see Japanese Sentai-forces and other national defenders becoming more of a trend than city-based defenders. We are arguably a more mobile population than in the 90s, and national or regional pride seems a bit more powerful of a force than hometown pride now. Outside of the US, I could see more German and French (or even EU, although that would be massively controversial) defenders than simply Berlin or Paris defenders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4732-drazosh","name":"Drazosh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T03:56:27-07:00","id":511870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492906-if-galatea-happened-today?p=493220#post493220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming an organization like Aeon existed, they'd have to step way more lightly in today's world of paranoia. If they randomly picked out some nova to recruit, all it takes is a single tweet and the suspicion would start flying. In an era where people are just looking for some kind of civil rights violation to raise hell about, if they did anything other than send info for how to apply for a job, they would never crawl out from under the internet's scrutiny. Big media spectacles like they did in the previous timeline would be picked apart in comment forums, and internet news blogs. They'd take apart that news coverage of Randall Portman like a lego castle.</div> </div> </div> </div>On an aside, a non-national group taking care of the Nova situation might be even more of a necessity in our oh-so-jaded with national governments' intrigue contemporary world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T04:46:00-07:00","id":512808,"title":"","content":"While a Dirty Dozen/Suicide Squad lends itself to a lot of good story hooks, i don't think there will be enough novas criminals for a decade or more. Eventually, yes. But not so soon after N-Day, going by those numbers i posted. I'd have to see a trustworthy breakdown, but i'd intuitively agree with Wolfgar about prison eruptees being mostly of a political variety (small charges spun into mandatory sentencing) and that many contemporary eruptees in the US and North Korea will personally know someone they may feel is wrongly imprisoned.<br /> Excellent call with Japanese Sentai Novas. As soon as there are five Novas in Japan there will be allusions anyway, it's just a matter of time before the contracts are signed. But maybe Bandai or Sony instead of the national diet could end up with the controls, whether the nova-infatuated Japanese public would let them get into dangerous fights might be another matter however. Certainly a project to tidy up Fukushima will be among the early actions of Japanese Novas, so a level of public endearment should stay on course with the setting material.<br /> I just can't see anyone supplying insurance for the noble municipal defender, not unless a solid legal framework was standardized to protect everyone involved against too much loss - corporations can go under from those kinds of costs. I like the municipal defenders, don't get me wrong, but i'm just having a hard time picturing how they could operate under the ultra litigious US culture. The EU has a more distributed power-structure and would be out-of-character to hang such responsibility on any single individual - but novas would likely rise to highly specialized positions in law enforcement over there - just maybe without as much celebrity attached. Just a guess, Europe has too many moving parts to accurately generalize this way. But nationalist eruptees in certain countries could spin into the EU breaking down over the next decade after N-Day - things are still pretty tense over there since the GFC.<br /> Finally, Baaldam makes a fine point about Aeon. How welcome would a non-profit, NGO with serious juice be in the echelons of power over the past few years? Of course, to really slip into the role, Aeon will need some major changes from how it appears in Adventure! and there will be resistance from incumbent powers. So i still think Aeon should start negotiations within a week a the latest (if the evidence is there by that stage), rather than wait a whole month before pushing for the Zurich Accord - thing move faster now then they did in '98.<br /> <br /> P.S. I'm starting to wonder if any of this extended thread has been of assistance to Sahugani?<br /> -smile-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T08:48:55-07:00","id":512957,"title":"","content":"if not Sahugani, perhaps we've been of assistance to the Devs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T11:43:36-07:00","id":526894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492906-if-galatea-happened-today?p=512957#post512957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if not Sahugani, perhaps we've been of assistance to the Devs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol, I'm kinda dumbfounded, I checked a day after I posted I think and just never managed to get back to it. Was a total a surprise to come back now and find you guys had actually run with it. Lots of great stuff here. Thanks for all the great ideas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5371-sahugani","name":"Sahugani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5371_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T12:30:34-07:00","id":526937,"title":"","content":"Glad to see we didn't stray too far off the topic, if there are any more specific questions i'm sure many of the same posters will take another punt. We were already starting to topple into a US-specific interpretation - propbably because that's where many posters hail from, or at least hear about twenty-four-seven due to all the meda produced there reaching the rest of the world (soft power).<br /> Anyway, thanks for the likes (i assume that was you liking all the posts in the thread, you politician. -tease-) and as a final bit of opinion i'd advise running the early years after N-Day as close to India and China geographically as you can due to the slow rate of eruptions elsewhere in the world. The first few years are going to be pretty mundane while the era picks up steam otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}